$DIR/main.p:47:7: cannot move (*p) out of the value p points to with the assertion (*p).(owned[Buf])
    The assertion (*p).(owned[Buf]) moves the value out of (*p). But the value
    belongs to whatever p points into, which would drop it again when it is
    dropped. Only a whole variable or a temporary can be asserted out of.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    Take the value out first, which leaves the zero value in (*p), and put back
    what you keep:
        v := take(p).(owned[Buf])
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3303" for a longer explanation)

